# <%~ it.instance.name || it.instance.slug %>: Appointment Case
<%
  /* The internal half of the `onboarding-approved` gate: the document whoever signs this stage
     off reads before doing so. Leads with the case for appointing this candidate, then the
     commitments made on the strength of it — offer, contract, payroll. It carries no approval
     section, because the approval is the sign-off on the stage this document belongs to. See
     definition.yaml.

     Payroll's rework section is `?` and suppresses entirely on a hire where validation passed
     first time, which is the outcome this process is aiming for and, per the source model, not
     the common one.

     v2 (#90): `selection.preferred-candidate` split into `candidate-name` (text, also what
     names this document — see definition.yaml's `filename:`) and `rationale` (markdown).
     `contract.start-date` is now a date, formatted here with `formatDate()` for human reading;
     what's stored on disk stays ISO. `contract.start-date-changes` is a new optional field. */
%>
# The appointment

## Role

<%~ na(it.modules.role.summary) %>

## Team and reporting line

<%~ na(it.modules.role.team) %>

## Engagement type

<%~ na(it.modules.engagement.type) %>

## Candidate name

<%~ na(it.modules.selection['candidate-name']) %>

## Selection rationale

<%~ na(it.modules.selection.rationale) %>

## Vetting outcome

<%~ na(it.modules.vetting.outcome) %>

# Offer

## Offer terms

<%~ na(it.modules.offer.terms) %>

## Status

<%~ na(it.modules.offer.status) %>
<% if (it.modules.offer.negotiation) { %>
## Negotiation

<%~ it.modules.offer.negotiation %>
<% } %>
# Contract

## Terms

<%~ na(it.modules.contract['terms-summary']) %>

## Signatures

<%~ na(it.modules.contract.signatures) %>

## Start date

<%~ na(formatDate(it.modules.contract['start-date'])) %>
<% if (it.modules.contract['start-date-changes']) { %>
## Start date changes

<%~ it.modules.contract['start-date-changes'] %>
<% } %>
# Payroll

## Details requested

<%~ na(it.modules.payroll['details-requested']) %>

## Validation outcome

<%~ na(it.modules.payroll['validation-outcome']) %>
<% if (it.modules.payroll.rework) { %>
## Rework

<%~ it.modules.payroll.rework %>
<% } %>
## Payroll confirmation

<%~ na(it.modules.payroll.confirmed) %>
<% if (it.modules['open-questions'].questions && it.modules['open-questions'].questions.length) { %>
# Open questions

<% it.modules['open-questions'].questions.forEach(function(item) { %>- <%~ item %>
<% }) %><% } %>
